{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73KmNLH4nx1YPRLkZB2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Install uv if you don't have it:\n\n```bash\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh   # macOS/Linux\n# or: pip install uv / brew install uv\n```\n\nThen create a project:\n\n```bash\nuv init myproject        # new directory\ncd myproject\n```\n\nOr use `uv init` inside an existing directory.\n\nThis creates `pyproject.toml`, `main.py`, `README.md`, `.python-version`, and a git repo.\n\n**Common next steps**\n\n```bash\nuv add requests          # add a dependency (creates .venv and uv.lock on first use)\nuv add --dev pytest      # add a dev dependency\nuv run main.py           # run your code in the project's environment\nuv run pytest            # run any command in the environment\nuv sync                  # install everything from the lockfile (e.g. after cloning)\nuv remove requests       # remove a dependency\n```\n\n**Useful `init` options**\n\n- `uv init --lib mylib`: library layout (`src/` package, build system included)\n- `uv init --package myapp`: packaged app with a `src/` layout and a CLI entry point\n- `uv init --python 3.12`: pin a Python version (uv downloads it if needed)\n- `uv init --bare`: just a `pyproject.toml`\n\nYou don't need to activate the venv manually. `uv run` handles it. If you want to anyway, use `source .venv/bin/activate`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6838,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6838},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c455bbf-7fa7-4fc8-93d9-981248d4dbb7","uuid":"5d722b19-23b1-4107-b172-f038b306b8a3","timestam